.TH MU2EDAQ\-DISCOVER 1 "2026-06-12" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-discover \- query the network for running Mu2e DAQ services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-discover
.RB [ \-\-filter
.IR KEY=GLOB ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-retries
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-group
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR ip ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-json | \-\-table ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-discover
multicasts a DISCOVER query (protocol
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery/1 ,
group 239.255.42.99, UDP port 28999) and prints every ANNOUNCE reply:
service name, application type, host, port, stable instance id, and
start time.
Replies are deduplicated by instance id across query retransmissions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " KEY=GLOB"
Restrict results.
Keys:
.BR app ", " name ", " host .
Values are fnmatch-style globs (e.g.\&
.BR app=vnc ,
.BR host=mu2e\-dl\-* ).
May be repeated; all filters must match.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Total time to wait for replies (default 2.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " n"
Number of query transmissions spread across the timeout window (default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-group " addr" ", " \-\-port " port"
Override the multicast group and UDP port.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " ip"
Local interface IP to send the multicast on (useful on multi-homed hosts).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
YAML config file with a
.B discovery:
section (keys
.BR group ", " port ", " timeout ).
Requires PyYAML.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print results as a JSON array instead of a table.
.SH CONFIGURATION PRECEDENCE
Command line options override the environment variables
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_GROUP ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_PORT ,
and
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT ,
which override the config file
.RB ( \-\-config
or
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG ),
which overrides built-in defaults.
.SH EXAMPLES
List everything on the local network segment:
.EX
    mu2edaq\-discover
.EE
Only VNC sessions, as JSON:
.EX
    mu2edaq\-discover \-\-filter app=vnc \-\-json
.EE
From off-site (multicast does not traverse the gateway):
.EX
    ssh \-J mu2egateway01.fnal.gov mu2edaq@mu2e\-dl\-01.fnal.gov \\
        mu2edaq\-discover \-\-json
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (including zero results); non-zero on invalid arguments or
protocol errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bootstrap (1)
.PP
Protocol specification:
.B doc/PROTOCOL.md
in the mu2edaq\-discovery repository.
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-discovery
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-discovery
.UE
